# PANESAR LIVING — Project rules for agent work

1. Preserve every pre-existing tracked and untracked change.
2. Never use `git reset`, `git clean`, destructive `git checkout`/`git revert`, or broad file overwrites.
3. Do not install dependencies, commit, push, or deploy without explicit authorization.
4. Default to frontend-only work for UI tasks.
5. Do not change backend, API, authentication, database, schema, migrations, or business logic without explicit authorization.
6. Preserve the six buildings (M1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5) and six rooms per building. Never change existing room/building IDs or assignments.
7. Preserve rent, payment, electricity, and collection behavior.
8. Audit first, implement second: never edit files during a read-only audit; wait for explicit approval before making changes.
9. For broad frontend tasks: inspect shared components once, group related presentation improvements into one coordinated pass, and validate the combined changes once.
10. Prefer the smallest coherent patch; review the diff; validate actual behavior.
11. Never claim a build, test, or browser check passed unless it actually ran.
12. If a task risks violating a protected boundary, stop and explain before proceeding.

Entry points: `frontend/src/App.jsx`, `frontend/src/components/shared.jsx`
Styling: `frontend/src/components.css`, `frontend/src/App.css`
Frontend scripts (run from `frontend/`): `npm run build`, `npm run lint`, `npm run test:contract`
